    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.surround\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThat's a simple one:\r\n\r\nWhen adding a surround in normal mode, it expects to select what thing to wrap around in what's to come\r\nPutting user in a state pretty much like the visual mode, as you can do any text object selection (like `iw`, `3j`, `t)`, etc)\r\n\r\nIt would be real nice if a that point, WhichKey could show what movements/selection are possible\r\n\r\nSo one can for example `sa` (WhichKey shows options) `a↓`\r\n\r\n\r\nThat one came up on a [issue on LazyVim](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/issues/2160), and i think would be really beneficial",
