            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> That's a simple one:\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, it is not.\r\n\r\nThe only way 'mini.surround' can add those kind of hints is to provide specific mappings for all kinds of textobjects (like `saiw`, `sa3j`, etc.), which is not feasible. Other than that, adding custom 'which-key.nvim' hints for Operator-pending mode is not a 'mini.surround' responsibility, I am afraid.\r\n\r\nLazyVim already [does have custom hints for 'mini.ai'](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/879e29504d43e9f178d967ecc34d482f902e5a91/lua/lazyvim/plugins/coding.lua#L210-L253) textobjects. So if you have 'mini.ai' active from LazyVim, you can press `gs` followed by one of `a` or `i` and it should show hints for that subset of textobjects. It is also not really possible to have descriptions for its targets inside of 'mini.ai' itself for reasons described in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/192#issuecomment-1442020792).\r\n\r\nThe reason it doesn't already have that for 'mini.surround' seems to be related to folke/which-key.nvim#469.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2023-12-16T10:04:18Z",
